    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the elite 81.26 score for **Trea Turner**. Facing Kay (L), **Trea Turner** benefits immensely from the SP skill adjustment (+18%) and his prime #2 slot in the order; with his penchant for high-volume production, he is our clear priority play. **Kyle Schwarber** follows closely with a 79.42, as his ability to leverage the platoon advantage against Kay makes him a primary source of power. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** carries a 75.84 rating, buoyed by a significant +14% park factor and an opportunistic matchup against Feltner that plays perfectly into his ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries for potential stolen bases\u2014a critical factor given our emphasis on the scarcest category.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on **Colt Keith**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 47.69 score. While **Colt Keith** holds value, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Lars Nootbaar** (64.02) and **Casey Schmitt** (60.89), both of whom benefit from favorable lineup positioning and stronger platoon alignments against their respective right-handed matchups. Elsewhere, **Junior Caminero** faces a tougher test against Gusto (2.88 xERA), resulting in a marginal 52.96 score, but his role at the top of the order remains vital. We continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, who remains unavailable as he logs time with the Oklahoma City Comets. \n\nWhile the majority of our lineup faces favorable splits, **Yordan Alvarez** (60.47) is a notable exception; despite a sub-elite SP skill matchup against Perkins, his exceptional 0.454 xwOBA keeps his floor high enough to warrant a start. Conversely, the benching of **Dillon Dingler** (38.61) was a mandatory move to protect our daily game caps, as his projected efficiency fell well below our 40-point threshold against Woo. Owners should keep a close eye on any late weather updates, as the aggressive utilization of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.67) and **Carson Benge** (58.10) assumes clean conditions to maintain their efficiency in the outfield.",
